    "['set policy-options policy-statement [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'bgp 100', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'bgp 100', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the translation of the Juniper BGP neighbor configuration to Huawei equivalent:\\n\\n##\\nbgp 100\\npeer 10.20.1.2 as-number 100\\npeer 10.20.1.2 connect-interface GigabitEthernet1/0/0\\n##\\n\\nNotes:\\n1. The Huawei command creates a BGP process with AS 100 (equivalent to Juniper's peer-as)\\n2. The neighbor is configured with the same AS number (100)\\n3. The connect-interface specifies the interface to use for the BGP session (ge-1/0/0 in Juniper is GigabitEthernet1/0/0 in Huawei)\\n4. Huawei uses a different command structure where BGP configuration is entered in BGP view\", 'trans_template': 'bgp 100'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'peer 10.20.1.2 as-number 100', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'peer 10.20.1.2 as-number 100', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the translation of the Juniper BGP neighbor configuration to Huawei equivalent:\\n\\n##\\nbgp 100\\npeer 10.20.1.2 as-number 100\\npeer 10.20.1.2 connect-interface GigabitEthernet1/0/0\\n##\\n\\nNotes:\\n1. The Huawei command creates a BGP process with AS 100 (equivalent to Juniper's peer-as)\\n2. The neighbor is configured with the same AS number (100)\\n3. The connect-interface specifies the interface to use for the BGP session (ge-1/0/0 in Juniper is GigabitEthernet1/0/0 in Huawei)\\n4. Huawei uses a different command structure where BGP configuration is entered in BGP view\", 'trans_template': 'peer 10.20.1.2 as-number 100'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'peer 10.20.1.2 connect-interface GigabitEthernet1/0/0', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'peer 10.20.1.2 connect-interface GigabitEthernet1/0/0', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the translation of the Juniper BGP neighbor configuration to Huawei equivalent:\\n\\n##\\nbgp 100\\npeer 10.20.1.2 as-number 100\\npeer 10.20.1.2 connect-interfac